      "settings": {
        "title": "",
        "jump_label": "On this page",
        "lede": "<p>Condition tells you how much life a card has lived. Every raw card in the shop is listed as one of five conditions, from Near Mint to Damaged. This guide explains each one in everyday words, so you know what to expect before a card arrives.</p><p>The descriptions follow TCGplayer's published conditioning standards, a common reference for buying and selling single cards.</p>"
      }
    },
    "tiers": {
      "type": "binder-condition-tiers",
      "blocks": {
        "tier_nm": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier": "nm",
            "code": "NM",
            "name": "Near Mint",
            "summary": "<p>The card looks like it went from the pack into a sleeve. Look very closely and you might find a speck of white on an edge or a faint scuff, and that's about it.</p>",
            "look_for_label": "What you might see",
            "look_for": "<ul><li><strong>Edges and corners:</strong> at most a tiny white speck or two, usually only visible on the dark blue back.</li><li><strong>Surface:</strong> a faint scuff or one light scratch that you have to tilt the card to find.</li><li><strong>Shape:</strong> perfectly flat. No bends, no dents you can feel.</li></ul>",
            "not_here_label": "Not at this level:",
            "not_here": "Creases, bends, dirt or grime, peeling, or any wear that shows without tilting the card.",
            "diagram_label": "Card back with one tiny white speck on the right edge"
          }
        },
        "tier_lp": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier": "lp",
            "code": "LP",
            "name": "Lightly Played",
            "summary": "<p>The card has been handled or played with care. Small signs of wear show up when you look for them, but nothing jumps out from arm's length.</p>",
            "look_for_label": "What you might see",
            "look_for": "<ul><li><strong>Edges and corners:</strong> a few small white nicks along the edges, or a corner that has lost a little color. The back shows this first.</li><li><strong>Surface:</strong> light scratches or scuffing, like a fine line across the holo that only appears when it catches the light.</li><li><strong>Shape:</strong> a slight bend can still be Lightly Played if it is small. A crease cannot.</li></ul>",
            "not_here_label": "Not at this level:",
            "not_here": "Creases, tears, splits in the surface, or anything that changes the card's shape.",
            "diagram_label": "Card back with a few white nicks on the edges and one corner, and a faint scratch"
          }
        },
        "tier_mp": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier": "mp",
            "code": "MP",
            "name": "Moderately Played",
            "summary": "<p>The card has clearly been used. Wear is easy to spot, but the card is whole and still looks good in a binder.</p>",
            "look_for_label": "What you might see",
            "look_for": "<ul><li><strong>Edges and corners:</strong> whitening along long stretches of the edges and on several corners.</li><li><strong>Surface:</strong> scratches and scuffing you can see without tilting, including on the holo.</li><li><strong>Shape:</strong> a visible bend, a small dent, or a tiny split in the surface.</li></ul>",
            "not_here_label": "Not at this level:",
            "not_here": "Tears, holes, water damage, writing, or a deep crease across the card.",
            "diagram_label": "Card back with whitening along long stretches of the edges, two worn corners and several scratches"
          }
        },
        "tier_hp": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier": "hp",
            "code": "HP",
            "name": "Heavily Played",
            "summary": "<p>A lot of wear: heavy whitening, scuffing across big areas, maybe a crease. It is still clearly the real card, and still in one piece.</p>",
            "look_for_label": "What you might see",
            "look_for": "<ul><li><strong>Edges and corners:</strong> whitening around most of the border and on every corner.</li><li><strong>Surface:</strong> scuffing or scratches over large parts of the front or back.</li><li><strong>Shape:</strong> a long bend (more than about 2&nbsp;cm, or three quarters of an inch), dents, or a crease line.</li></ul>",
            "not_here_label": "Not at this level:",
            "not_here": "Anything that tears, punctures or splits the card, or hides its text.",
            "diagram_label": "Card back with whitening on all edges and corners, a large scuffed area and a crease line"
          }
        },
        "tier_dmg": {
          "type": "tier",
          "settings": {
            "tier": "dmg",
            "code": "DMG",
            "name": "Damaged",
            "summary": "<p>Wear goes past Heavily Played, or something has broken the card itself. Damaged cards can still be lovely binder copies for the right price, so look closely at the photos and the listing notes.</p>",
            "look_for_label": "What you might see",
            "look_for": "<ul><li>Tears, holes, punctures, or a fold that breaks the card.</li><li>Water damage, stains, writing, stickers or tape residue.</li><li>A crease that cuts across the card, or text that is missing or unreadable.</li><li>A big miscut or printing problem that affects the card itself.</li></ul>",
            "not_here_label": "Not at this level:",
            "not_here": "",
            "diagram_label": "Card back with a tear on the right edge, a crease from corner to corner and a water stain"
          }
        }
      },
